## PR Title
Support basic global constraints (#6551)

## PR Description
Implements the global-constraints feature defined in IEEE 1800-2023 section 18.5.8, addressing issue #6551. The implementation has three main pieces:

1. Global-constraint detection: an `isGlobalConstrained` flag is added to AstVar to identify variables participating in global constraints.
2. Constraint hoisting: constraints from nested member classes are extracted and evaluated together at the top-level class so that cross-object constraint solving works.
3. MemberSel handling: logic for nested member-access paths (e.g. `m1.inner.val`) is added so the SMT variable declaration is correct.

The author noted a memory leak issue early on which was addressed via subsequent refinements. The feature was developed across many commits between Sep 19 and Nov 5, 2025.

